body.translated_text:
Having smeared with cow dung a square ritual ground (<s>sthaṇḍila</s>) the size of a cowhide, one should make a mark upon it the length of an arrow. [Then:] with '<s>satyam asi</s>' (you are truth) one draws a northward line from the western half;
with '<s>ṛtam asi</s>' (you are cosmic order) an eastward line from the southern half;
with '<s>gharmam asi</s>' (you are the hot [milk]) an eastward line from the northern half;
two or three eastward [lines] in the middle;

children.translated_text:
'You are named <s>Yukti</s> (union);
you are named <s>Yoga</s> (connection);
you are named <s>Mati</s> (thought);'

body.translated_text:
Then he makes an oblation [with the mantras:]
'You are named <s>Āpvā</s>; may I attain your fulfillment;
I have grasped wisdom from the father, from the immortal;
I have shone forth like the sun;
<s>Svāhā</s>!'
'You are named <s>Āpva</s>; of that, of you...'
